 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Mutual Fund Analytics - Day 2: Database Operations & SQL Queries\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to the **Day 2 Notebook**! Today, we will execute the data cleaning pipeline, load the cleaned datasets into our structured SQLite relational database, validate the data constraints, execute 5 core analytical SQL queries, and plot visualizations to extract key business insights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Environment Setup\n",
    "First, we set up Python's system path to access modules in our custom `src/` directory and import libraries like `pandas`, `sqlite3`, `matplotlib`, and `seaborn`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find the folder where this notebook is, and get its parent folder (the project root)\n",
    "notebook_dir = Path.cwd()\n",
    "project_root = notebook_dir.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "if str(project_root) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.append(str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import sqlite3\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 6)\n",
    "print(\"Environment setup completed successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Clean Data & Re-Load Database\n",
    "We run the cleaning pipeline and rebuild the SQLite relational database from our cleaned datasets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scripts.data_cleaning import run_all_cleaning\n",
    "from scripts.database_loading import run_database_loading\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"--- Running Data Cleaning Pipeline ---\")\n",
    "run_all_cleaning()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Initializing and Loading SQLite Database ---\")\n",
    "run_database_loading()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Run Programmatic Database Validation\n",
    "Let's execute the validation checks to verify table existence, row counts, foreign key integrity, and sanity rules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scripts.database_validation import run_database_validation\n",
    "\n",
    "success = run_database_validation()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDatabase Validation Passed? {success}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Execute Analytical SQL Queries\n",
    "We connect to the database and execute each of the 5 analytical queries defined in `sql/queries.sql`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "db_path = project_root / \"data\" / \"db\" / \"mutual_fund_analytics.db\"\n",
    "conn = sqlite3.connect(str(db_path))\n",
    "conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\")\n",
    "print(f\"Connected to database at: {db_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Query 1: Assets Under Management (AUM) Analysis\n",
    "Rank fund houses by their latest AUM."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query_1 = \"\"\"\n",
    "WITH latest_date AS (\n",
    "    SELECT MAX(date) AS max_date FROM fact_aum\n",
    ")\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    fund_house,\n",
    "    date,\n",
    "    aum_crore,\n",
    "    aum_lakh_crore,\n",
    "    num_schemes,\n",
    "    RANK() OVER (ORDER BY aum_crore DESC) as aum_rank\n",
    "FROM fact_aum\n",
    "WHERE date = (SELECT max_date FROM latest_date)\n",
    "ORDER BY aum_crore DESC;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "df1 = pd.read_sql_query(query_1, conn)\n",
    "df1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Query 2a & 2b: Transaction summaries and payment modes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query_2a = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    transaction_type,\n",
    "    COUNT(*) as transaction_count,\n",
    "    SUM(amount_inr) as total_amount_inr,\n",
    "    ROUND(AVG(amount_inr), 2) as average_amount_inr\n",
    "FROM fact_transactions\n",
    "GROUP BY transaction_type\n",
    "ORDER BY total_amount_inr DESC;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "query_2b = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    payment_mode,\n",
    "    COUNT(*) as transaction_count,\n",
    "    SUM(amount_inr) as total_amount_inr,\n",
    "    ROUND(COUNT(*) * 100.0 / (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM fact_transactions), 2) as transaction_pct\n",
    "FROM fact_transactions\n",
    "GROUP BY payment_mode\n",
    "ORDER BY transaction_count DESC;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df2a = pd.read_sql_query(query_2a, conn)\n",
    "df2b = pd.read_sql_query(query_2b, conn)\n",
    "display(df2a)\n",
    "display(df2b)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Query 3: Performance Metrics (Top Performing Funds)\n",
    "Find top funds with a Sharpe ratio > 1.0, ranked by 3-year return."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query_3 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    amfi_code,\n",
    "    scheme_name,\n",
    "    fund_house,\n",
    "    category,\n",
    "    return_3yr_pct,\n",
    "    return_5yr_pct,\n",
    "    sharpe_ratio,\n",
    "    morningstar_rating\n",
    "FROM fact_performance\n",
    "WHERE sharpe_ratio > 1.0\n",
    "ORDER BY return_3yr_pct DESC;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "df3 = pd.read_sql_query(query_3, conn)\n",
    "df3.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Query 4: SIP Inflow Trends\n",
    "Month-over-month growth in industry SIP inflows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query_4 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    month,\n",
    "    sip_inflow_crore,\n",
    "    sip_inflow_crore - LAG(sip_inflow_crore) OVER (ORDER BY month) as mom_change_crore,\n",
    "    ROUND((sip_inflow_crore - LAG(sip_inflow_crore) OVER (ORDER BY month)) * 100.0 / LAG(sip_inflow_crore) OVER (ORDER BY month), 2) as mom_growth_pct,\n",
    "    active_sip_accounts_crore,\n",
    "    new_sip_accounts_lakh\n",
    "FROM fact_sip_industry\n",
    "ORDER BY month;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "df4 = pd.read_sql_query(query_4, conn)\n",
    "df4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Query 5: Portfolio Diversity (Dominant Sector per Scheme)\n",
    "Find the top sector allocation for each fund scheme."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "query_5 = \"\"\"\n",
    "WITH ranked_sectors AS (\n",
    "    SELECT \n",
    "        p.amfi_code,\n",
    "        f.scheme_name,\n",
    "        p.sector,\n",
    "        SUM(p.weight_pct) as total_weight_pct,\n",
    "        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY p.amfi_code ORDER BY SUM(p.weight_pct) DESC) as sector_rank\n",
    "    FROM fact_portfolio p\n",
    "    JOIN dim_fund f ON p.amfi_code = f.amfi_code\n",
    "    GROUP BY p.amfi_code, p.sector\n",
    ")\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    amfi_code,\n",
    "    scheme_name,\n",
    "    sector as dominant_sector,\n",
    "    ROUND(total_weight_pct, 2) as dominant_sector_weight_pct\n",
    "FROM ranked_sectors\n",
    "WHERE sector_rank = 1\n",
    "ORDER BY dominant_sector_weight_pct DESC;\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "df5 = pd.read_sql_query(query_5, conn)\n",
    "df5.head(10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5: Visualizations\n",
    "Let's plot premium visual charts for our reports."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. AUM Ranking\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df1, x=\"aum_crore\", y=\"fund_house\", palette=sns.color_palette(\"coolwarm\", len(df1)))\n",
    "plt.title(\"AUM Ranking by Fund House (Crores)\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=15)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"AUM (INR Crore)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Fund House\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2. Transactions volume & value by type\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df2a, x=\"transaction_type\", y=\"transaction_count\", ax=axes[0], palette=\"Blues_d\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Transaction Count by Type\", fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df2a[\"total_amount_cr\"] = df2a[\"total_amount_inr\"] / 1e7\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df2a, x=\"transaction_type\", y=\"total_amount_cr\", ax=axes[1], palette=\"Purples_d\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Total Transaction Value (Crores)\", fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Transaction Type Volume vs Value\", fontsize=15, fontweight=\"bold\", y=0.98)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 3. Payment Mode pie chart\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "plt.pie(df2b[\"transaction_count\"], labels=df2b[\"payment_mode\"], autopct='%1.1f%%', \n",
    "        startangle=140, colors=sns.color_palette(\"pastel\"), wedgeprops=dict(width=0.4, edgecolor='w'))\n",
    "plt.title(\"Transaction Volume Breakdown by Payment Mode\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=15)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4. SIP Inflow trends\n",
    "fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "sns.lineplot(data=df4, x=\"month\", y=\"sip_inflow_crore\", marker=\"o\", color=\"#1a73e8\", linewidth=2.5, ax=ax1)\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "ax1.set_title(\"Industry SIP Inflow Trends & Growth\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=15)\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel(\"SIP Inflow (INR Crore)\", color=\"#1a73e8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n",
    "df4_growth = df4.dropna(subset=[\"mom_growth_pct\"])\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df4_growth, x=\"month\", y=\"mom_growth_pct\", ax=ax2, alpha=0.3, color=\"#34a853\")\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel(\"MoM Growth Rate (%)\", color=\"#34a853\")\n",
    "ax2.grid(False)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 5. Dominant sector allocations\n",
    "df5_head = df5.head(10)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df5_head, x=\"dominant_sector_weight_pct\", y=\"scheme_name\", hue=\"dominant_sector\", dodge=False, palette=\"Set2\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Dominant Sector Allocations (Top 10 Schemes)\", fontsize=14, fontweight="bold", pad=15)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Sector Weight (%)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Scheme Name\")\n",
    "plt.legend(title=\"Dominant Sector\", loc=\"lower right\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "conn.close()\n",
    "print(\"Database connection closed.\")"
   ]
  }
